---
// The headline spans the full container: in a type-led fold the type IS the
// composition, so constraining it to a column leaves the other half dead.
//
// Sizing is bounded so each sentence fits one line at desktop. At 22 characters
// and -0.04em tracking each line needs about 10.5em of width, so the 6.5rem
// ceiling clears the 1232px content box with room to spare. Below ~500px the
// lines wrap — that is expected, the two-line rule is a desktop constraint.
---

<h1
  id="hero-title"
  class="hero-enter text-[clamp(2.25rem,8vw,6.5rem)] font-bold leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.04em] text-white"
>
  <span class="block">Tu dirección en Miami.</span>
  <span class="block text-accent-400">Compras sin fronteras.</span>
</h1>
